// === QUESTION TEXT ===
<p>The Simplex Candle Shop makes two kinds of candles: <b>votives</b> and <b>pillars</b>. Let `x` be the number of votives produced and `y` the number of pillars produced each day.</p>

<p>Each votive uses `$a1` ounces of wax and `$a2` minutes of labor. Each pillar uses `$b1` ounces of wax and `$b2` minutes of labor. The shop has `$c1` ounces of wax and `$c2` minutes of labor available each day.</p>

<p>Each votive earns a profit of `$$p1` and each pillar earns a profit of `$$p2`. The shop wants to maximize daily profit</p>

<p style="text-align:center">`P = $p1 x + $p2 y`</p>

<p>subject to the wax and labor constraints and `x >= 0`, `y >= 0`.</p>

<p>Set up the initial simplex tableau, carry out the simplex method, and read the optimal solution from the final tableau.</p>

<p>(a) How many votives should the shop make each day? `x =` $answerbox[0]</p>

<p>(b) How many pillars should the shop make each day? `y =` $answerbox[1]</p>

<p>(c) What is the maximum daily profit? `P = $` $answerbox[2]</p>

