<p>`A^{-1} =` $answerbox[0]</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> Use the inverse method, `X = A^{-1}B`, to solve the system. Enter the solution vector `X`.</p>
<p>`X =` $answerbox[1]</p>

// === ANSWER ===
$solutionguide = '<p><strong>Step 1 - Find the determinant of A.</strong> Expanding along the first row,</p>'
 . '<p>`det(A) = ' . $a11 . '(' . $a22 . '*' . $a33 . ' - ' . $a23 . '*' . $a32 . ') - ' . $a12 . '(' . $a21 . '*' . $a33 . ' - ' . $a23 . '*' . $a31 . ') + ' . $a13 . '(' . $a21 . '*' . $a32 . ' - ' . $a22 . '*' . $a31 . ') = ' . $det . '`</p>'
 . '<p>Since `det(A) = ' . $det . ' != 0`, the inverse exists.</p>'
 . '<p><strong>Step 2 - Build the adjugate matrix.</strong> Take the cofactor of each entry, then transpose. Dividing every entry of the adjugate by `det(A) = ' . $det . '` gives</p>'
 . '<p>`A^{-1} = ' . $answer[0] . '`</p>'
