<ol type="a">
<li>`log_{$b1}({$v1})` = $answerbox[0]</li>
<li>`log_{$b2}({$v2})` = $answerbox[1]</li>
<li>`log_{$b3}(1/{$v3})` = $answerbox[2]</li>
</ol>

<p>For part c, remember that a reciprocal can be rewritten with a negative exponent, so that answer will be negative.</p>

// === ANSWER ===
$solutionguide = "<p><strong>Part a.</strong> Ask what power of {$b1} gives {$v1}. Since {$b1}<sup>{$e1}</sup> = {$v1}, we get log base {$b1} of {$v1} equals {$e1}.</p><p><strong>Part b.</strong> Ask what power of {$b2} gives {$v2}. Since {$b2}<sup>{$e2}</sup> = {$v2}, we get log base {$b2} of {$v2} equals {$e2}.</p><p><strong>Part c.</strong> Rewrite the fraction with a negative exponent: 1 over {$v3} equals {$b3}<sup>-{$e3}</sup>. So log base {$b3} of 1 over {$v3} equals -{$e3}.</p>";

// === NAME - DESCRIPTION:  ===
