// === NAME - DESCRIPTION: handshakes-pairwise-count - Counts pairwise handshakes among n people with C(n,2), recounts after the group grows, and identifies what counting ordered pairs without halving represents ===
// === SET QUESTION TYPE TO: multipart ===

// === COMMON CONTROL ===
$n = rand(8,20);
$nm1 = $n - 1;
$prod = $n*$nm1;
$h = $prod/2;

$k = rand(2,5);
$nt = $n + $k;
$ntm1 = $nt - 1;
$h2 = $nt*$ntm1/2;

$anstypes = "number,number,choices";

$answer[0] = $h;
$answer[1] = $h2;

$questions[2] = array(
"Every handshake counted twice, once from each of the two people in it",
"Every handshake counted exactly once",
"Every handshake counted once for each person in the room",
"Each person counted shaking their own hand as well as every other hand"
);
$answer[2] = 0;

// === QUESTION TEXT ===
<p>At a meeting of $n colleagues, every pair of colleagues shakes hands exactly once.</p>

<p>Part a. How many handshakes take place in all? $answerbox[0]</p>

<p>Part b. Before any handshaking begins, $k more colleagues arrive, so there are $nt people in the room. Every pair of people in the room then shakes hands exactly once. How many handshakes take place now? $answerbox[1]</p>

<p>Part c. A classmate answers Part a by multiplying $n by $nm1 and stopping there, without dividing by 2. What has the classmate counted? $answerbox[2]</p>

// === ANSWER ===
$solutionguide = "<p>Step 1 — Count ordered pairs. Each of the $n colleagues shakes hands with $nm1 others, which gives $n times $nm1 = $prod ordered pairs of people.</p>
<p>Step 2 — Remove the double count. Every handshake appears twice in that list, once as A shaking B and once as B shaking A, so the number of handshakes is $prod divided by 2, which is $h. This is the same as the combination count of choosing 2 people from $n.</p>
<p>Step 3 — With $k more colleagues there are $nt people, so the count becomes $nt times $ntm1 divided by 2, which is $h2.</p>
<p>Answer: Part a is $h. Part b is $h2. Part c: multiplying $n by $nm1 and stopping counts every handshake twice, once from each end, which is why the product must be halved.</p>";

// === NAME - DESCRIPTION: Compound interest, monthly compounding: compute the future value of a principal at an annual rate over a term, rounded to the cent ===
