// === QUESTION TEXT ===
<p>A hiker walks along a straight trail. The function</p>
<p style="text-align:center">`D(t) = $a t^2 + $b t`</p>
<p>gives the hiker's distance from the trailhead, in miles, `t` hours after the hike began. The hiker starts at 7:00 a.m. and finishes the hike $H hours later.</p>
<p><strong>(a)</strong> Find the hiker's distance from the trailhead $t1 hours after starting. Enter only the number, in miles.</p>
<p>$answerbox[0]</p>
<p>///</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> What is the domain of `D` in this situation?</p>
<p>$answerbox[1]</p>
<p>///</p>
<p><strong>(c)</strong> Find the average rate of change of `D` on the interval `$t2 <= t <= $t3`. Enter only the number, in miles per hour.</p>
<p>$answerbox[2]</p>

// === ANSWER ===
$s1 = "D($t1) = $a($t1)^2 + $b($t1) = " . ($a*$t1*$t1) . " + " . ($b*$t1) . " = $dt1";
$s3 = "D($t3) - D($t2) = $dt3 - $dt2 = " . ($dt3-$dt2);
$s3b = "($dt3 - $dt2) / $runLen = " . ($dt3-$dt2) . " / $runLen = $aroC";

$solutionguide = '<p><strong>Step 1: Evaluate the model at '.$t1.' hours.</strong> Replace every `t` with '.$t1.'.</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>`'.$s1.'`</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>So the hiker is '.$dt1.' miles from the trailhead.</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p><strong>Step 2: State the domain.</strong> The model describes the hike only from the moment it starts, `t = 0`, until the moment it ends, `t = '.$H.'`. The distance is defined at both of those moments, so both endpoints are included. The domain is the interval from 0 to '.$H.' hours inclusive, written `[0, '.$H.']`. Choosing all real numbers would describe a hike with no start and no end. Choosing the open interval from 0 to '.$H.' would throw away the starting and finishing distances, which the model does give. Choosing from 0 hours onward with no end would let the hike run forever.</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p><strong>Step 3: Average rate of change on `'.$t2.' <= t <= '.$t3.'`.</strong> Subtract the distances and divide by the length of the time interval.</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>`'.$s3.'`</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>`'.$s3b.'`</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>The average rate of change is '.$aroC.' miles per hour. Because `D` is quadratic, this value is the slope of the line joining the two points on the graph; it is not the speed at any single instant.</p>';

