// === QUESTION TEXT ===
<p>A print shop charges a setup fee plus a per-book printing cost, so the <b>average cost per book</b>, in dollars, for an order of `x` books is given by</p>

<p style="text-align:center">`A(x) = $k/x + $b`</p>

<p><b>Part a.</b> Find the average cost per book when an order contains `$p` books. Give your answer in dollars, rounded to two decimal places if needed.</p>

<p>$answerbox[0]</p>

<p><b>Part b.</b> In the context of this problem, which of the following is the appropriate domain for the function `A`?</p>

<p>$answerbox[1]</p>

<p><b>Part c.</b> Find the average rate of change of `A` on the interval `[$a, $c]`. Round to two decimal places if needed.</p>

<p>$answerbox[2]</p>

// === ANSWER ===
$solutionguide = '<p><b>Step 1 - Evaluate the function at x = ' . $p . '.</b></p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>Substitute ' . $p . ' for `x`: `A(' . $p . ') = ' . $k . '/' . $p . ' + ' . $b . ' = ' . ($k/$p) . ' + ' . $b . ' = ' . $ansEval . '`</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>So the average cost is $' . $ansEval . ' per book.</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p><b>Step 2 - Find the domain.</b></p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>The formula has `x` in the denominator, so `x` cannot equal 0. But `x` is the number of books in an order, and an order must contain at least one book. So the appropriate domain in this context is all positive values of `x`, that is `x > 0`.</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p><b>Step 3 - Compute the average rate of change on the interval.</b></p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>Find the function values at the two endpoints:</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>`A(' . $c . ') = ' . $k . '/' . $c . ' + ' . $b . ' = ' . ($k/$c) . ' + ' . $b . ' = ' . ($k/$c + $b) . '`</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>`A(' . $a . ') = ' . $k . '/' . $a . ' + ' . $b . ' = ' . ($k/$a) . ' + ' . $b . ' = ' . ($k/$a + $b) . '`</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>Then divide the change in `A` by the change in `x`:</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>`(A(' . $c . ') - A(' . $a . '))/(' . $c . ' - ' . $a . ') = (' . ($k/$c + $b) . ' - ' . ($k/$a + $b) . ')/' . ($c - $a) . ' = ' . $ansAroc . '`</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>The average rate of change is negative, which means the average cost per book falls as the order size increases from ' . $a . ' to ' . $c . ' books.</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p><b>Answer:</b> Part a: ' . $ansEval . ' dollars per book. Part b: all positive values of `x`. Part c: ' . $ansAroc . ' dollars per book per additional book.</p>';

