$solutionguide .= '<li>Part c: `k = ' . $k3 . '`, so `1 - 1/(' . $k3 . '^2) = ' . round(1 - 1/($k3**2), 6) . '`. As a percent that is at least ' . $r3 . ' percent.</li>';
$solutionguide .= '</ul>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>Step 3 &mdash; Read part d carefully. The rule says <em>at least</em>, never <em>exactly</em>. Two data sets with the same mean and standard deviation can put very different shares of their observations inside `\mu - 2\sigma` to `\mu + 2\sigma`: a bell shaped set puts about 95 percent there, while a set with a few far outliers can put well over 95 percent there. So the exact share depends on the shape of the data, and the rule only guarantees a floor.</p>';
