$zc = randfrom(array(-1.7,-1.5,-1.3,-1.1,-0.9,-0.6,-0.4,0.4,0.6,0.9,1.1,1.3,1.5,1.7));
$c = round($meanSum + $zc*$seSum);

$z = ($c - $meanSum)/$seSum;
$prob = 1 - normalcdf($z,0,1);

$zR = round($z,2);
$probR = round($prob,4);
$seSumR = round($seSum,4);
$belowR = round(normalcdf($z,0,1),4);

$anstypes = array("number","number");
$answer[0] = $prob;
$answer[1] = $seSum;
$abstolerance[0] = 0.001;
$abstolerance[1] = 0.001;

// === QUESTION TEXT ===
<p>A courier service has found that the time needed to deliver a package is approximately normally distributed with mean `$mu` minutes and standard deviation `$sigma` minutes. The deliveries are independent of one another.</p>

<p>A dispatcher selects `$n` deliveries at random and records the total delivery time `T = x_1 + x_2 + ... + x_n` for those deliveries.</p>

<p>(a) Find the probability that the total delivery time for the `$n` deliveries is greater than `$c` minutes. Round your answer to 4 decimal places.</p>
<p>`P(T > $c) =` $answerbox[0]</p>

<p>(b) Find the standard deviation of the sampling distribution of `T` in minutes.</p>
<p>$answerbox[1]</p>

// === ANSWER ===
$solutionguide = '<p>Step 1 - Mean of the total. The total of n independent delivery times has mean</p><p>`mu_T = n*mu = '.$n.' * '.$mu.' = '.$meanSum.'` minutes.</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>Step 2 - Standard deviation of the total. Variances add, so the standard deviation of the total is</p><p>`sigma_T = sigma*sqrt(n) = '.$sigma.' * sqrt('.$n.') = '.$seSumR.'` minutes. This is the answer to part b.</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>Step 3 - Standardize the cutoff. The total is normally distributed, so</p><p>`z = ('.$c.' - '.$meanSum.') / '.$seSumR.' = '.$zR.'`</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>Step 4 - Use the standard normal curve. The probability of exceeding the cutoff is the area to the right of z, which is</p><p>`P(T > '.$c.') = 1 - P(Z < '.$zR.') = 1 - '.$belowR.' = '.$probR.'`</p>';
$solutionguide .= '<p>Answer: the probability is about '.$probR.', and the standard deviation of the total is '.$seSumR.' minutes.</p>';

