// === QUESTION TEXT ===
<p>A study of social media use asked a random sample of $sampleSize students at a large university how many minutes per day they spend on social media. From the data the researchers reported a 95% confidence interval for `mu`, the mean number of minutes per day for all students at the university:</p>

<p style="text-align: center;">`($lower, $upper)` minutes</p>

<p>A campus wellness group claims that the population mean is $hypo minutes per day. You will test `H_0: mu = $hypo` against `H_a: mu != $hypo` at the 5% significance level, using the reported interval.</p>

<p><b>a.</b> Give the margin of error of the reported interval, in minutes. $answerbox[0]</p>

<p><b>b.</b> What is the decision of this test at the 5% significance level? $answerbox[1]</p>

<p><b>c.</b> Choose the best conclusion in the context of this study. $answerbox[2]</p>

// === ANSWER ===
$solutionguide = '';
$solutionguide .= '<p><b>Step 1 -- Find the margin of error.</b> A confidence interval for a mean is the sample mean plus or minus the margin of error, so the interval is centered at the sample mean and its half-width is the margin of error. ';
$solutionguide .= 'The midpoint of ' . $lower . ' and ' . $upper . ' is `bar x = ' . $center . '` minutes, ';
$solutionguide .= 'and the margin of error is half the width: `ME = (' . $upper . ' - ' . $lower . ') / 2 = ' . $margin . '` minutes. ';
$solutionguide .= 'So the interval can be written as `' . $center . ' +- ' . $margin . '`.</p>';

$solutionguide .= '<p><b>Step 2 -- Compare the hypothesized value with the interval.</b> ';
$solutionguide .= 'A 95% confidence interval for `mu` lines up with a two-sided test of `H_0: mu = ' . $hypo . '` against `H_a: mu != ' . $hypo . '` at the 5% significance level. ';
$solutionguide .= 'The rule is exact: reject `H_0` when the hypothesized value falls outside the interval, and fail to reject `H_0` when the value falls inside the interval.</p>';

if ($outcome == 1) {
  $solutionguide .= '<p>The value ' . $hypo . ' lies outside the interval from ' . $lower . ' to ' . $upper . '. ';
  $solutionguide .= 'At the 5% level, ' . $hypo . ' is therefore not a plausible value for the population mean. The decision is to reject `H_0`.</p>';
  $solutionguide .= '<p><b>Step 3 -- State the conclusion.</b> At the 0.05 level of significance there is convincing evidence that the mean daily time on social media for all students at the university differs from ' . $hypo . ' minutes.</p>';
} else {
  $solutionguide .= '<p>The value ' . $hypo . ' lies inside the interval from ' . $lower . ' to ' . $upper . '. ';
  $solutionguide .= 'At the 5% level, ' . $hypo . ' is still a plausible value for the population mean. The decision is to fail to reject `H_0`.</p>';
  $solutionguide .= '<p><b>Step 3 -- State the conclusion.</b> At the 0.05 level of significance there is not enough evidence to conclude that the mean daily time on social media for all students at the university differs from ' . $hypo . ' minutes. ';
  $solutionguide .= 'Failing to reject `H_0` does not show that the mean equals ' . $hypo . ' minutes. It only means the data are consistent with that value, so a difference that small could still be present.</p>';
}

